MINOR-4 — SIG-3 EAGAIN threshold decoupled from SIG-2 thread-utilisation context
======================================================================

Fix history (documented honestly, §11.4.6 — the first draft was CAUGHT
regressing SIG-3's own RED fixture BEFORE landing, per §11.4.4
test-interrupt-on-discovery):

  Draft 1 (REJECTED after testing): raise SIG-3's required EAGAIN hit-count
  when SIG-2's CURRENT thread utilization reads low. Running
  verify_resource_pressure_polarity.sh against this draft flipped SIG-3
  from "RED CONFIRMED" to "RED NOT REPRODUCED" — SIG-2 measures a
  POINT-IN-TIME "right now" state while SIG-3 looks BACK over a
  15-minute log window, so a genuine EAGAIN cascade that already
  subsided by the time SIG-2 is read would have been silently
  suppressed — the exact false-negative class §11.4.101's
  conservative-safe-default forbids. See the caught failing transcript
  this fix superseded: EFFECTIVE_SIG3_THRESHOLD raised to 10, a 4-hit
  real cascade (the fixture's own genuine artifact) no longer tripped it.

  Final fix (landed): the FAIL condition is UNCHANGED
  (SIG3_EAGAIN_THRESHOLD, sensitive by design) — MINOR-4's decoupling
  concern is closed by attaching a SIG-2 CONFIDENCE label
  ("elevated-current-SIG-2-or-unresolved" vs
  "SIG-2-not-currently-elevated") to the SIG-3 message and failure
  reason, so an operator sees the correlation context at a glance
  without ANY loss of detection sensitivity in either direction.

Full re-run below proves ALL FIVE signatures — including SIG-3 with the
final fix applied — still genuinely fire on their real pathological
artifact (§11.4.115(F)):

